# TL Commerce SaaS

Multi-tenant Laravel 9 e-commerce (`stancl/tenancy`). Work from repo root `c:\laragon\www\tlcommercesaas`.

## Structure (short)

- `Core/` — shared admin/core (blog, media, tenants, system)
- `plugins/` — modular features; main commerce = `tlecommercecore`, SaaS = `saas`, marketplace = `multivendor`
- `themes/tlcommerce/` — Vue 3 storefront; source in `resources/js/`, builds to `public/js/`
- `app/`, `routes/`, `config/` — standard Laravel + tenancy wiring

## Key Files

- `themes/tlcommerce/resources/js/layouts/MainLayout.vue` — root storefront layout; controls top-level structure and is the entry point for layout-aware rendering
- `themes/tlcommerce/resources/js/store/modules/layout.js` — Vuex module; provides `isSplitScreen` and `isMobile` getters used across all layout-conditional components

## Layout System

The storefront supports multiple tenant layouts driven by the Vuex `layout` module:
- Layout type is fetched at runtime from `/api/theme/tlcommerce/v1/get-active-layout`
- `isSplitScreen` getter returns `true` when `activeLayout.type === 'split_screen'`
- `isMobile` getter returns `true` when the viewport is mobile
- Components use `mapGetters(['isSplitScreen', 'isMobile'])` to access these values
- The standard conditional pattern is:

```vue
<template v-if="isSplitScreen && !isMobile">
  <!-- split-screen layout branch -->
</template>
<template v-else>
  <!-- default/original layout branch -->
</template>
```

## Merge Convention (3-file context tasks)

When given three versions of a Vue component:
- **Original** — untouched CodeCanyon file → becomes the `v-else` branch
- **Production** — working split-screen version → becomes the `v-if="isSplitScreen && !isMobile"` branch
- **Current** — developer's incomplete merge attempt → read for intent only, never copy directly

Merge rules:
1. `<template>` — wrap original in `v-else`, wrap production in `v-if="isSplitScreen && !isMobile"`
2. `<script>` — merge both scripts; `mapGetters` comes from production; no logic duplication
3. `<style>` — keep production custom styles AND original styles; add comments marking which belongs to which layout; resolve any selector conflicts
4. `mapGetters` must always include both `isSplitScreen` and `isMobile`

## Hard Rules

- **NEVER run `npm run dev`, `npm run development`, `npm run build`, or any npm/mix build command** — the developer reviews code changes first and runs the build manually
- Do not hand-edit compiled bundles under `themes/tlcommerce/public/js/`
- Do not modify `layout.js` store unless explicitly asked
- Do not modify `MainLayout.vue` unless explicitly asked
- Plugin PHP lives under `plugins/<name>/src/` with Blade in `views/`